## 2. Three live submitter fields

| Field | Values |
|-------|--------|
| Public Main Analysis | `Fixable` / `Invalid/Not Fixable` / `Valid as-is` |
| Internal Validity | `Invalid` / `Fixable` / `Valid-as-is` |
| Duplicate Analysis | `Fixable` / `Invalid/Not Fixable` / `Valid-as-is` |

Public must match Duplicate semantically. Internal is separate; record an evidence-based reason. Do not infer Internal from Duplicate. Block final answers if Public ≠ Duplicate.

---

## 3. Nine-case rule

All nine Internal Validity × Duplicate Analysis combinations remain supported. Duplicate Analysis alone selects the conditional branch.

---

## 4. Duplicate-controlled branch table

| Duplicate Analysis | Action |
| ------------------ | ------ |
| Fixable | Audit → correct `working_copy/` only → validate → flat corrected ZIP after preflight |
| Invalid/Not Fixable | Audit → diagnose → evidence ZIP (not a corrected valid ZIP) |
| Valid-as-is | Audit → seven confirmations → no task changes → no new ZIP |

---

## 5. Reviewer decision table

| Outcome | When |
|---------|------|
| Accept | Accurate complete submission |
| Needs Revision | Correctable defects remain and revision cycles available |
| Reject | Maximum revisions exhausted and Needs Revision unavailable |

Reviewer Mode is read-only. No task edits. No corrected ZIP. Optional targeted checks in a disposable copy only.

---

## 6. Canonical Harbor structure

```text
instruction.md
task.toml
environment/Dockerfile
environment/repo/
environment/problem_statement.md   # exact copy of instruction.md
solution/solve.sh
solution/golden.patch               # current canonical name
tests/test.sh
tests/tests.patch
tests/config.json
runs/                               # optional evidence; never upload
# Dialect-optional (never blocking): tests/grade.py, tests/files/, docker_compose.yaml
```

Legacy needing review/normalization: `solution/solution.patch`, `solution/init_state.patch`, `tests/files/`. Missing `init_state.patch` alone is not a defect. Missing `tests/grade.py` alone is not a defect.

